# --- Not published ------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/ is version-controlled: the frozen source of truth is the most valuable
# artifact here and a local-only copy is a single point of failure.
# The task trail under docs/work/ is raw material for the design and evaluation
# chapters, so it stays tracked. .claude/ (the workflow tooling) is local-only
# since 2026-10-27.
.claude/

# Submitted prose stays off a public remote: a public copy of text that is also
# handed in can register as a plagiarism-detection match against its own author.
docs/learning/
# Moved out of docs/learning/ on 2026-09-22 and so no longer covered by the rule
# above. It is the same submitted prose and this remote is public.
docs/Final_Proposal.md
# The final report: chapter drafts, LaTeX source, diagrams. The most submitted prose of all
# (2026-10-25). Ignored means no history here, so keep a private backup of it.
docs/0-Thesis-Report/

# --- Corpus -------------------------------------------------------------------
# dev-v0 is author-written (worklog W05, 2026-08-15) — freely releasable, and
# tracking it keeps the W5/W6 results reproducible.
# v1 stays out until data-card.md §1's redistribution TODO is resolved: the
# Amazon-Reviews-2023 dataset card states no license and this remote is public.
# Un-ignore once the terms are verified, or ship a download+build script and a
# hash manifest instead of the raw data.
data/v1/
# v1-draft is the same unresolved licence, one directory earlier in the pipeline.
# 175 files from the retired fetch script (wrong dataset) were once staged here by mistake. The
# Amazon-PQA builder (experiments/scripts/build_pqa.py) writes data/v1-draft/pqa/ and is the only
# thing that should; regenerate it with `make pqa-build`, never track it.
data/v1-draft/
# Raw Amazon-PQA source files, as downloaded. Redistribution is NOT granted (the
# dataset's own readme carries the ACM personal/classroom notice) and this remote
# is public, so these never get tracked — permanently, not pending a licence check.
# Not under data/v1/: rag.ingest globs that directory. Hashes live in docs/data-card.md §1
# and in build_pqa.py (a test checks the two are equal).
data/raw/
# The workload (item 3.4): the whole file and its two split files hold Amazon-PQA question text,
# so they are the same unresolved licence. Ignored before the first one is written. The tracked
# record is data/workload-manifest.json (sha256s and counts, no text), re-included below; regenerate
# the files with the workload-* make targets. Every version is covered, not only v1 (review F7).
data/workload-*.json
!data/workload-manifest.json
# The dataset epoch file and its lock (item 4.2, ADR-008): one integer that changes with every ingest
# and every edit. Machine state, not corpus; `make epoch-advance` creates it.
data/dataset-epoch
data/dataset-epoch.lock

# --- Build output --------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated protobuf stubs (regenerate with `make proto`)
gateway/internal/ragpb/
rag/src/rag/pb/

# Go
gateway/gateway
gateway/bin/
*.test

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Experiment figures regenerate from raw/ via `make figures`
experiments/results/*/figures/

# Run raw output is NOT published. requests.jsonl carries verbatim Amazon-PQA question text
# (query_raw) and raw/answers/ holds LLM answers grounded on PQA chunks; redistribution is not
# granted and this remote is public (docs/data-card.md, ADR-005). manifest.yaml stays tracked.
# Decided 2026-10-06 (docs/work/2026-10-06-answer-text-storage/approvals.md, decision 5).
experiments/results/*/raw/

# --- OS ------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store

# --- demo UI -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source is tracked; the toolchain output is not. `make ui` regenerates dist/ from
# source, so shipping it would be a second copy of the same thing that can drift.
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
